/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_ReleaseV1 Foundation v1.0.0 Backlog
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_Validation
 * @brief Version-controlled plan and release gates for Foundation v1.0.0.
 *
 * This page is the source of truth for Foundation v1.0.0 readiness. Update it
 * in the same commit that changes a task's status or acceptance evidence. Do
 * not maintain a separate progress copy in chat, a spreadsheet, or a Gantt.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Status Status Header
 *
 * | Field | Value |
 * | ----- | ----- |
 * | Target | `v1.0.0` |
 * | Working branch | `main` (trunk-based development) |
 * | Overall status | `IN PROGRESS` |
 * | Current milestone | M1 - Release contract |
 * | Last reviewed | 2026-09-25 |
 * | Release decision | Not ready |
 *
 * Allowed task states are:
 *
 * | State | Meaning |
 * | ----- | ------- |
 * | `NEXT` | The next task to execute. |
 * | `TODO` | Accepted scope, not started. |
 * | `IN PROGRESS` | Work exists locally or on a branch but is not accepted. |
 * | `BLOCKED` | Cannot continue until the recorded dependency is resolved. |
 * | `DONE` | Acceptance criteria passed and evidence is recorded. |
 * | `DEFERRED` | Explicitly removed from the v1.0.0 scope. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Rules Update Rules
 *
 * - Keep task IDs stable so commits and conversations can refer to them.
 * - Change a task to `DONE` only after all stated acceptance criteria pass.
 * - Record evidence as a commit SHA, CI run, command log, package inspection,
 *   consumer build, or hardware-validation record.
 * - A successful cross-compilation is not evidence of target execution.
 * - A test run that discovers zero tests is not a passing test result.
 * - When scope changes, mark the task `DEFERRED` and explain why; do not delete it.
 * - Update the status header and release gates whenever this backlog changes.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Roadmap Dependency Roadmap
 *
 * This dependency roadmap is intentionally used instead of a dated Gantt. Add
 * calendar dates only after runner and hardware availability is known.
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph FoundationReleaseV1Roadmap {
 *     rankdir=TB;
 *     graph [
 *         bgcolor="transparent",
 *         pad="0.25",
 *         nodesep="0.55",
 *         ranksep="0.65"
 *     ];
 *     node [
 *         shape=box,
 *         style="rounded,filled",
 *         color="#34495e",
 *         fontcolor="#17202a",
 *         fontname="Helvetica",
 *         fontsize=11,
 *         margin="0.18,0.12"
 *     ];
 *     edge [
 *         color="#5d6d7e",
 *         penwidth=1.5,
 *         arrowsize=0.8
 *     ];
 *
 *     M1 [label="M1\nRelease contract", fillcolor="#d6eaf8"];
 *     M2 [label="M2\nContinuous integration", fillcolor="#d6eaf8"];
 *     M3 [label="M3\nTest depth and code quality", fillcolor="#fcf3cf"];
 *     M4 [label="M4\nPackage and workflow hardening", fillcolor="#fcf3cf"];
 *     M5 [label="M5\nPlatform and hardware validation", fillcolor="#fadbd8"];
 *     M6 [label="M6\nRelease candidate and v1.0.0", fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];
 *
 *     M1 -> M2;
 *     M2 -> M3;
 *     M2 -> M4;
 *     M3 -> M5;
 *     M4 -> M5;
 *     M5 -> M6;
 *
 *     { rank=same; M3; M4; }
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Baseline Completed Baseline
 *
 * | ID | State | Deliverable | Evidence |
 * | -- | ----- | ----------- | -------- |
 * | BASE-001 | `DONE` | Pre-v1 scripts, presets, toolchains, and workflow baseline | `943c192` |
 * | BASE-002 | `DONE` | Modular GoogleTests and cross-platform example layout | `33ca3c7` |
 * | BASE-003 | `DONE` | Release-only exported packages | `96c0892` |
 * | BASE-004 | `DONE` | Auto-discovered interactive example launchers | `f2786cc` |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M1 M1 - Release Contract
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | V1-001 | P0 | `DONE` | Define the support matrix | Every public preset is classified in @ref Foundation_BuildGuide_SupportMatrix; PIC is deferred and unvalidated candidates cannot be called supported. |
 * | V1-002 | P0 | `DONE` | Make version and language requirements consistent | CMake, `library.properties`, and source mode report 1.0.0; CMake rejects version drift; the current Debug and Release suites each pass 108 tests; direct source mode accepts C++17 and rejects C++14; Doxygen rebuild passes. |
 * | V1-003 | P0 | `BLOCKED` | Confirm the distribution license | Interim state is `All Rights Reserved / No License Granted`; README prohibits external use and identifies the project as proprietary. A qualified legal expert must review ownership, prior grants, contribution terms, and the final distribution model before release. |
 * | V1-004 | P0 | `DONE` | Audit and freeze the public API | All 16 findings have documented dispositions; 108 Debug and 108 Release tests pass on `macos_arm64`; the isolated exported-package consumer links out-of-line API through `Foundation::Foundation`. See @ref Foundation_Workflows_PublicApiAudit. |
 * | V1-005 | P1 | `TODO` | Add release history and limitations | `CHANGELOG.md` contains the 1.0.0 scope and the documentation lists known limitations. |
 *
 * M1 exits when the public contract no longer contradicts the build and every
 * advertised platform has an explicit support level.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M2 M2 - Continuous Integration
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | CI-001 | P0 | `TODO` | Add native build and test CI | GitHub-hosted Linux, macOS, and Windows jobs build and run non-zero Debug and Release test suites. Windows covers MSVC and Clang; Linux covers GCC and Clang. |
 * | CI-002 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate exported packages in CI | Every native job performs a fresh Release export and a separate `find_package` consumer links `Foundation::Foundation`. |
 * | CI-003 | P1 | `TODO` | Validate documentation on pull requests | Doxygen builds before merge and fails on structural errors or unresolved references; deployment remains a main-branch operation. |
 * | CI-004 | P1 | `TODO` | Add embedded compile jobs | ARM and AVR jobs configure, build Debug/Release, export Release, and inspect archive identity without pretending to execute target code. |
 * | CI-005 | P1 | `TODO` | Preserve useful failure evidence | CI uploads logs, test reports, and selected package artifacts needed to reproduce a failure. |
 *
 * Docker may support Linux and cross-compiler jobs. It does not replace native
 * Windows/MSVC or macOS runners.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M3 M3 - Test Depth and Code Quality
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | TEST-001 | P0 | `TODO` | Inventory public API coverage | Every public type/function maps to a test, compile check, documented exception, or target-only validation. |
 * | TEST-002 | P0 | `TODO` | Complete Math tests | Complex, fixed/dynamic matrices, matrix operations, arithmetic, trigonometry, Ratio, and numeric edge cases are covered. |
 * | TEST-003 | P0 | `TODO` | Complete remaining module tests | Containers, Functional, Time, Scheduling, TypeTraits, and Utils include empty, full, invalid, boundary, and lifecycle behavior where applicable. |
 * | TEST-004 | P1 | `TODO` | Add public-header self-containment checks | Each supported public header compiles in an otherwise minimal translation unit. |
 * | TEST-005 | P1 | `TODO` | Add warning and sanitizer jobs | Supported native compilers run an agreed warning set; AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer pass where available. |
 * | TEST-006 | P1 | `TODO` | Finish the coverage workflow | Coverage uses a supported compiler, produces a readable report, records a baseline, and has an agreed release threshold; otherwise the public option is removed from v1.0.0. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M4 M4 - Package and Workflow Hardening
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | PKG-001 | P0 | `DONE` | Add a repository-owned package consumer fixture | `tests/PackageConsumer` is isolated from the source tree, validates umbrella and selective includes, links out-of-line Time symbols through the imported target, and passed a fresh `macos_arm64` export on 2026-09-25. See @ref Foundation_Workflows_PackageConsumer. |
 * | PKG-002 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate the feature-option matrix | Default, full, each top-level module disabled, and core-only configurations either pass or fail at configure time with a precise dependency error. |
 * | PKG-003 | P1 | `TODO` | Harden clean and fresh-state behavior | Release validation cannot accidentally reuse stale tests, examples, metadata, or binaries from an earlier configuration. |
 * | PKG-004 | P0 | `TODO` | Verify artifact identity | Each package contains one Release archive, correct headers/metadata, no Debug import, and the expected compiler/architecture/ABI identity. |
 * | PKG-005 | P1 | `TODO` | Validate Arduino source mode | At least the declared Arduino/AVR board compiles the documented sketches from the source layout; untested cores are not advertised as validated. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M5 M5 - Platform and Hardware Validation
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | VAL-001 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate macOS arm64 | Complete Debug, Release, tests, examples, export, architecture inspection, launcher, and external consumer checklist. |
 * | VAL-002 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate macOS x64 | Cross-build and inspect x86-64 artifacts; run tests/consumer through Rosetta or on Intel hardware. |
 * | VAL-003 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate Windows MSVC x64 | Complete both configurations, non-zero tests, Release export, launcher, archive inspection, and external consumer. |
 * | VAL-004 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate Windows Clang x64 | Complete the same evidence using the Clang preset and toolchain. |
 * | VAL-005 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate Linux x64 | GCC and Clang CI jobs complete both configurations, package checks, and consumers. |
 * | VAL-006 | P1 | `TODO` | Validate Linux arm64 / Raspberry Pi | Native GCC/Clang build, tests, export, and consumer pass on an Arm64 Linux environment. |
 * | VAL-007 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate AVR ATmega328P | Debug/Release compile, Release package, consumer ELF, size/architecture inspection, and board or emulator smoke result are recorded. |
 * | VAL-008 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate STM32 | All advertised profiles compile and package; at least one real firmware consumer links and executes on representative hardware. |
 * | VAL-009 | P1 | `TODO` | Decide PSoC 5LP status | Exact PSoC toolchain/consumer evidence promotes it to supported; otherwise v1.0.0 explicitly marks it experimental. |
 *
 * Store each platform's command log using the record format in
 * @ref FoundationValidationReport. The checklist in
 * @ref Foundation_Workflows_DesktopValidation remains the detailed procedure;
 * this backlog records release status rather than duplicating its commands.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M6 M6 - Release Candidate and Final Release
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | REL-001 | P0 | `TODO` | Freeze release documentation | README, Doxygen, changelog, support table, license, examples, and package instructions match the candidate. |
 * | REL-002 | P0 | `TODO` | Publish `v1.0.0-rc.1` | RC tag is created from a clean, green commit and no new features enter after the tag. |
 * | REL-003 | P0 | `TODO` | Re-run the complete release matrix | Required CI, local platform, package-consumer, and hardware evidence passes on the exact RC commit. |
 * | REL-004 | P0 | `TODO` | Publish `v1.0.0` | Main contains the approved candidate; annotated tag, release notes, target packages, and checksums are published and downloadable. |
 * | REL-005 | P0 | `TODO` | Prove downstream readiness | A clean external project consumes the released tag/package without repository-relative paths or unreleased files. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Gates Release Gates
 *
 * Every item below must be checked before `v1.0.0`:
 *
 * - [ ] All P0 tasks are `DONE`; remaining P1 tasks are either `DONE` or
 *       explicitly `DEFERRED` with a documented limitation.
 * - [ ] The support matrix matches collected evidence.
 * - [ ] Required CI is green on the exact release commit.
 * - [ ] Native Debug and Release tests execute and pass; zero tests is rejected.
 * - [ ] Release packages contain no Debug artifacts.
 * - [ ] Separate consumers link the installed packages.
 * - [ ] Required embedded archive, firmware-link, and hardware evidence exists.
 * - [ ] Documentation builds and contains no known release contradiction.
 * - [ ] Qualified legal review has approved the final license, copyright
 *       ownership, contribution terms, and intended distribution model.
 * - [ ] The worktree is clean and the release can be reproduced from a clean clone.
 * - [ ] Release notes, packages, and checksums are ready before creating the final tag.
 */
